# RetailOps V1 rules

## Authority
Use this order of authority:
1. docs/PRODUCT-CONTRACT.md and docs/TECHNICAL-HANDOFF.md when present.
2. The approved RetailOps screen copy and route contract in the active Cursor prompt.
3. The working app under apps/pos-web.
4. reference/make-prototype only as a visual and interaction reference.

Never edit reference/make-prototype.

## Scope
V1 includes front counter, storeroom and minimal admin only.
Do not add owner dashboards, general reports, inventory analytics, purchasing, accounting, supplier tools or competitor intelligence.

## Staff usability
- Staff open directly into work, not a dashboard.
- One obvious primary action per screen.
- Use literal staff language.
- Hide diagnostics under More details or manager-only views.
- Preserve unfinished work.
- Every error must explain the next safe action.

## Locked corrections to the Make prototype
- Remove dashboard-first routing.
- Remove EFT.
- F12 means Take payment, not Lock register.
- Never store or compare plaintext PINs in production code.
- Do not hard-code employees, products or completed orders inside App.tsx.
- Do not claim Shopify, printer or card-terminal success without an explicit confirmed state.
- Use ZAR and integer cents.
- Prices are VAT-inclusive at 15%; do not add VAT on top of the displayed selling price.
- Measured quantities use integer tenths of a metre; never use binary floating point for money or measured inventory.
- A paid sale is recorded locally before background Shopify update.
- Storeroom work must not wait for Shopify.

## Code quality
- TypeScript strict mode.
- Small files and explicit domain types.
- Separate UI, domain, state and external adapters.
- No external calls directly from presentation components.
- Validate all consequential inputs.
- Add tests for money, measured quantities, payment allocation and order-state transitions.
- Do not add dependencies unless required and justified in the change report.

## Security
- Shopify tokens and secrets remain server-side.
- PINs must be salted and hashed server-side before pilot.
- Never commit secrets or real customer data.
- All payment confirmation, refunds, corrections, approvals and cash-up closure require audit records.
